# There is no single .env at the repo root — each app has its own, because the
# split is a security boundary rather than a convention:
#
#   apps/api/.env         → see apps/api/.env.example
#                           Every secret lives here. The FastAPI backend is the
#                           only process in the product with a runtime.
#
#   apps/web/.env.local   → see apps/web/.env.local.example
#                           NEXT_PUBLIC_* values only. apps/web is a static
#                           export, so anything set here is inlined into the
#                           browser bundle and is therefore public.
#
# Copy each example into place beside it:
#
#   cp apps/api/.env.example apps/api/.env
#   cp apps/web/.env.local.example apps/web/.env.local
#
# Production values are not kept in either file: the backend's are set in the
# Render dashboard (declared, without values, in render.yaml) and the frontend's
# are Cloudflare Pages build variables mirrored in apps/web/wrangler.toml.
